#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091970 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "cb7d8dc0-98eb-53d0-9e48-3b1c2d7f6308" :question/math-academy-id "e-4508" :question/problem "Find a solution to the system of linear equations\n\n${2x + y = 2; 4x + 3y = 6$." :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA^{-1} &= \\frac{1}{3 \\cdot 2 - 4 \\cdot 1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &= A^{-1}b \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solution is $x=0$ and $y=2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091971 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/id #uuid "422d31ad-8caa-5ce2-a0e0-c905fcc2640d" :question/math-academy-id "e-4509" :question/problem "Solve the system of linear equations\n\n${2x - 3y = 5; 6y - 5x =-8$." :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{2x - 3y = 5; - 5x + 6y =-8\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form\n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{x} =\\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA^{-1} &= \\frac{1}{6 \\cdot 2 - 3 \\cdot 5}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &= A^{-1}b \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=-3$."}]}
